FINDING (saved to runs/ml/causal_dwell.log): both arms are strictly causal and share one
  dwell and one zero-false-alarm operating point, so neither gets lookahead.
  READ THE n COLUMN FIRST. 30 realisations are attempted per cell, but a pair survives
  only when BOTH arms alarm, and the paired n falls to 5-19 wherever they do not. The
  point estimates at +10 and 0 dB are computed on those survivors and the censoring is
  not random -- it is the same informative-attrition problem as the IMM arm of Table I.
  Exactly ONE cell shows a resolved positive advantage: matched short-time at +20 dB,
  +6.0 ms, CI [+5.0,+6.5], p=0.003, n=30/30 -- about 18% of the 34 ms budget. At +10 and
  0 dB the matched estimates (-1, -20 ms) are NOT resolved: their intervals span zero on
  n=19 and n=9. The narrowband 3-10 Hz arm resolves nothing positive at any SNR, and at
  a 150 ms dwell / 0 dB it is resolved NEGATIVE (-119.5 ms, p=0.027).
  Resolving 4-8 Hz needs >=2 cycles (250-500 ms) against a ~34 ms event, so no dwell
  choice serves both -- the fin cue is a velocity burst, not a tone.
  CONCLUSION: the ~34 ms fin-to-onset interval is an INFORMATION BUDGET a causal
  detector cannot spend. The +28 ms in physical_cue_test.py came from rendering the muD
  arm from the instantaneous state against a comparator with no dwell: WITHDRAWN.
  See study/HANDOFF_2026-07-25_FALSIFICATION.md section 4d.
